Subject: [PATCH] ubifs: a name that is not in a directory is not found

ubifs_finddir returned -ENOENT at the end of a directory, which its caller
took for a match: looking up a file that is not there succeeded, and loading
it read the directory above it (seen on a W1700K: ubifsload of a deleted
file "Done", 160 bytes of nothing). The end of the directory is 0, not found.

--- a/fs/ubifs/ubifs.c
+++ b/fs/ubifs/ubifs.c
@@ -492,0 +493,3 @@
+	/* The end of the directory is no entry of that name, which 0 says. */
+	if (ret < 0)
+		ret = 0;
